---
// The hosted playmat's limits: what it keeps, when games are dropped, how
// to keep a game's record, how many players it serves and how many
// requests a minute. The numbers come from the App Platform definition
// (lib/facts.ts), so they change when it does: the stat tiles under the
// intro hold them (the data-limit values), and the text repeats them.
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import Prompt from '../../components/Prompt.astro';
import { limits, site } from '../../lib/facts';
---
<Docs
  title="The hosted playmat's limits"
  description="What the hosted tcgreplay playmat keeps, when games are dropped, and how many players and requests it serves."
>
  <h1>The hosted playmat's limits</h1>
  <p>
    The hosted playmat at {site.publicURL.replace('https://', '')} is free and small. It runs on a single server, so it keeps games only in
    memory and serves a limited number of players at once. Here is what that means for you.
  </p>
  <ul class="tiles" data-limit-tiles>
    <li class="tile"><span class="value">1</span> <span class="what">game per account at a time</span></li>
    <li class="tile"><span class="value" data-limit="idle">{limits.idleTimeout}</span> <span class="what">without activity before a game is dropped</span></li>
    <li class="tile"><span class="value" data-limit="users">{limits.maxUsers}</span> <span class="what">players signed in at once</span></li>
    <li class="tile"><span class="value" data-limit="rate">{limits.requestsPerMinute}</span> <span class="what">requests a minute per account</span></li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="what-it-keeps">What it keeps</h2>
  <p>
    Each Google account has <strong>one game at a time</strong>, held in the playmat's memory: the imported battle log,
    the moves on the board, its branches and the assistant's coaching notes. Importing or starting another game replaces
    it. See <a href="/privacy">privacy</a> for everything it keeps about you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="when-games-are-dropped">When games are dropped</h2>
  <ul class="rows">
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"></path></svg>
      <span>After <strong>{limits.idleTimeout}</strong> without activity. The next time your assistant
      uses the game, it is told the game expired.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12a8 8 0 1 0 2.4-5.7"></path><path d="M4 4v4.5h4.5"></path></svg>
      <span><strong>Whenever the playmat is updated or restarted</strong>, which can happen at any time: every change to
      tcgreplay is deployed straight away, and every game is lost when it is.</span>
    </li>
    <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 4h4v16h-4"></path><path d="M10 8l-4 4 4 4"></path><path d="M6 12h10"></path></svg><span>When your last sign-in ends.</span></li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="keep-the-record">Keep the record</h2>
  <p>
    To come back to a game later, ask your assistant for its <strong>record</strong> and keep it somewhere safe, such as
    a note. The record holds the battle log, both decklists and everything needed to rebuild the game exactly.
  </p>
  <Prompt text="Give me this game's record so I can keep it." />
  <p>
    Later, paste the record into a chat and ask your assistant to import it: the same game comes back, move for move.
    Branches you made and coaching notes aren't part of the record.
  </p>

  <h2 id="players-and-requests">How many players and requests</h2>
  <ul class="rows">
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="8" r="3.5"></circle><path d="M2.5 20a6.5 6.5 0 0 1 13 0"></path><path d="M16 4.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7"></path><path d="M18 14.5a6.5 6.5 0 0 1 3.5 5.5"></path></svg>
      <span>It serves up to <strong>{limits.maxUsers}</strong> signed-in players at once. A place is freed
      when a player's game is dropped or their last sign-in ends.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 18a8 8 0 1 1 16 0"></path><path d="M12 18l4-6"></path></svg>
      <span>Each account may make up to <strong>{limits.requestsPerMinute}</strong> requests a minute, from
      the assistant and the board together. Normal play stays well under it.</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="messages">Messages you may see</h2>
  <dl class="messages">
    <div>
      <dt>"tcgreplay is busy"</dt>
      <dd>
        The playmat already has {limits.maxUsers} players signed in. Your assistant may say "the server is busy: it already
        has the most signed-in users it serves at once ({limits.maxUsers}); try again later". Try again later, or run it
        on your desktop (below).
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>"too many requests"</dt>
      <dd>
        Your account went over {limits.requestsPerMinute} requests a minute: "too many requests: this account is limited
        to {limits.requestsPerMinute} requests a minute; try again in …s". Wait the few seconds it says and carry on.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>"Your game expired"</dt>
      <dd>
        The game was dropped after {limits.idleTimeout} without activity. Import its record again to carry on.
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <h2 id="when-full">When it's full: run it on your desktop</h2>
  <p>
    The playmat is open source and runs on your own computer with the Claude desktop app, with no sign-in and no limits,
    and your games stay on your machine. See <a href="/docs/desktop">running it on your desktop</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>

<style>
  /* The numbers: one tile each, the value large in the mono face. */
  /* Two by two: the article is too narrow for four abreast with the idle
     time spelled out. */
  .tiles { list-style: none; margin: var(--space-6) 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); }
  .tile {
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--panel);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--line);
  }
  .value { font: 600 var(--fs-28) / 1.1 var(--font-mono); color: var(--primary); }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .value { font-size: var(--fs-22); }
  }
  .what { font-size: var(--fs-14); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  /* When games are dropped, and players and requests: a white row each,
     with its icon. */
  .rows { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .rows li {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding: 14px var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
    background: var(--panel);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--line);
  }
  .rows svg {
    flex: none;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    margin-top: 4px;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--primary);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  /* Messages you may see: a card each, the message in amber mono. */
  .messages { margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .messages > div {
    padding: 14px var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
    background: var(--panel);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--line);
  }
  .messages dt { font: 600 var(--fs-14) var(--font-mono); color: var(--warn-ink); }
  .messages dd { margin: 6px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
